+.TH pkgconfig n 8.5 Tcl "Tcl Built-In Commands"
+.so man.macros
+.BS
+'\" Note:  do not modify the .SH NAME line immediately below!
+.SH NAME
+tcl::pkgconfig \- query the build configuration of Tcl
+.SH SYNOPSIS
+\fBtcl::pkgconfig list\fR
+.sp
+\fBtcl::pkgconfig get \fIkey\fR
+.BE
+.SH DESCRIPTION
+.PP
+The \fBtcl::pkgconfig\fR command returns information about how the Tcl
+library was configured and built. It is created by \fBTcl_RegisterConfig\fR
+(see its manual page); packages may provide the same command in their own
+namespace, for example \fBtk::pkgconfig\fR.
+.TP
+\fBtcl::pkgconfig list\fR
+.
+Returns a list of the names of all defined keys.
+.TP
+\fBtcl::pkgconfig get \fIkey\fR
+.
+Returns the value associated with \fIkey\fR. An error is raised if the key
+is not known.
+.SH KEYS
+.PP
+The boolean keys (values \fB0\fR or \fB1\fR) are \fBdebug\fR (built with
+symbols), \fBthreaded\fR, \fBprofiled\fR, \fB64bit\fR (configured with
+\fB\-\-enable\-64bit\fR), \fBoptimized\fR, \fBmem_debug\fR,
+\fBcompile_debug\fR and \fBcompile_stats\fR.
+.PP
+The path keys come in two forms: \fIname\fB,install\fR is the location
+chosen at installation time and \fIname\fB,runtime\fR the location the
+library uses at run time. \fIname\fR is one of \fBlibdir\fR,
+\fBbindir\fR, \fBscriptdir\fR, \fBincludedir\fR and \fBdocdir\fR. The
+key \fBdllfile,runtime\fR gives the file name of the Tcl shared library.
+.SH EXAMPLE
+.CS
+puts "Tcl scripts are in [\fBtcl::pkgconfig get\fR scriptdir,runtime]"
+.CE
+.SH "SEE ALSO"
+Tcl_RegisterConfig(3), tm(n)
+.SH KEYWORDS
+configuration, build

